WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.790
A churchyard on the edge of the moor.

2
00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:07.500
A freshly dug grave, a spade,
and an older grave beside it.

3
00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:11.290
Years after Catherine's death,
Heathcliff comes back here,

4
00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:13.150
and opens her coffin.

5
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.780
Now rewind.

6
00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:18.050
A small boy, found in
the streets of Liverpool.

7
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.480
Words land around him,
and none of them are kind.

8
00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:25.900
Then the boy grows into a tall
man, full of ledgers and keys.

9
00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:29.270
So how can anyone pity a
man who does such things?

10
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:32.550
In this mission, you'll hear
how others name the child,

11
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:33.790
and treat him.

12
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.960
You'll follow how he turns their weapons,

13
00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:38.560
debts and marriages, against them.

14
00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:42.060
And you'll hear his grief
on the night Catherine dies.

15
00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:45.900
Your mission: explain why
readers still pity him.
